{
  "summary": "LibreOffice Impress provides several view options to create, edit, and organize presentations. By default, Impress opens in Normal view, which is used for creating and editing slides. Users can also change slide designs from the Master Pages section in the Tasks pane. Outline view displays slide contents and headings arranged like a table, allowing presenters to reorganize text items up, down, or across lines. Slide Sorter view enables easy reordering of slides into any desired sequence through simple drag-and-drop operations. Notes view allows presenters to add speaker notes that remain visible on the presenter's monitor during a slideshow while staying hidden from the audience. Finally, the Tasks pane, which can be toggled via the View menu, contains a Layout section for modifying individual slide layouts, such as applying the Content over Content layout. Each view can be accessed either from the View menu or via its dedicated tab.",
